WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.701
-Welcome back.
You look fantastic, as always.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.067
I'm so happy when you come on
the show.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:07.200
Thank you for coming on.
-I love being here.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.901
-I want to show a picture that
Drake posted on Instagram.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.701
A picture of you and Drake.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:16.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.100
And no big deal.
You guys are hanging out.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.767
And he said, "Fill it up
in a briefcase

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:26.834
and split that shiz
with my vibe."

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:28.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.267
That's pretty cool.
Do you have any idea what --

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:32.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:33.534
Do you have any idea
what that means?

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:34.901
-Well, I didn't know shiz.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.968
Now that I see it written,
now I know what that means.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:39.067
-Oh, yeah.
-S-dot-dot-dot.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.667
-Yeah.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:41.801
-No, I have no idea.

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:44.367
But he's charming.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:47.133
-Yes.
-And it must not be bad.

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:48.334
-No, it sounds good.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.067
-He would never write anything
bad about me.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.834
[ Laughter ]
-No, he wouldn't.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:56.501
"Fill it up with a briefcase
and split that S with my vibe."

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:57.801
I would do that.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:01.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.734
Where were you?

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:06.367
-Well, we were at
the CFDA Awards.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:09.434
And we were -- we had sat
at the same table.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:12.434
And we were all wearing
chrome hearts, you know,

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:14.968
all that really fabulous
jewelry.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:18.300
And I remarked that his hairdo
was very nice.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.367
And he started to
complain about it.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:22.868
Patted the top, and said it was
a little frizzy.

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.667
And I said
he looked really good.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:27.400
But men, I guess, worry about
their hairdos also.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.901
Do you worry about your hairdo?

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.167
-No, no.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.133
This is the best toupee
I can get on Amazon.

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.701
[ Laughter ]
It's really the greatest.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.901
He looks fantastic. Oh, yeah,
he was trying a new look?

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.100
-He's so charming.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.133
-But you were giving an award to
Kim Kardashian.

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.901
-I was, yeah.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.801
-And I also saw --
-For underwear.

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:45.234
-Yeah.
She did a great job with that.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:48.067
I saw a post that Kris Jenner
put up

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:50.801
of you guys with Khloe and Kris.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.300
-We all look the same. Look.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.300
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.367
You look like sisters.
-Yeah, we look exactly the same.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:00.367
-What was it like
at the Kardashians?

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.100
-Oh, fabulous.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.634
They live sort of in a compound.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:08.133
-They do, yeah.
-And they have very nice houses,

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.734
many rooms, all kinds of --

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:14.801
like 150 Hermes pocketbooks
in a closet.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.501
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:18.200
Did you get to snoop around
or anything?

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.300
-I got to go into every closet,
every refrigerator,

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.367
into basements, attics --

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:25.968
Well, they don't have an attic,
but --

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.667
-Yeah, you went everywhere.
-Everywhere.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.000
And we had such a good time.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.901
A very nice house tour.
-Yeah, I like that family.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:34.434
Is there any celebrity that
you get star-struck meeting?

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:37.467
-Meeting?
Well, if I could meet --

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:40.033
I was asked this question once.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:43.167
I've been sort of fascinated
with this very handsome

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:46.067
young boy on Instagram.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.801
He's called Brad Pitt.

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:51.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:55.467
And I -- I just sort of melt
when I look at those pictures.

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:57.801
I mean, he is so cute.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:58.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.133
-Really? For real, you --

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:02.000
-Oh, I mean, check it out.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:06.167
-I will.
But you follow Brad Pitt?

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.534
-I do.
-Were they fan pages?

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.834
-They're fan pages, I guess.
I don't know.

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.734
But whatever it is,

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:16.868
he looks better and better
as the years go by.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:19.300
-I love that you love Brad Pitt.
-I do. I do.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.267
-The holidays are coming up.
I always think of you.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.501
You're very nice to come on
our show

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.200
every holiday,
every Thanksgiving.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.934
And I do think of you.
Are you hosting a big party?

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:31.300
-I'm having a small --
no, small, small dinner.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.334
Just for orphans, people
who have nowhere else to go.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.367
So I thought it would be nice.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.968
[ Applause ]
-That's cool.

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.367
-Yeah.

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.167
-Is there a side dish to
Thanksgiving

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:45.000
that you think is
a little overrated?

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.934
-String beans.
-Yeah.

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:49.467
-Yeah. I mean,
even on the "Today" show,

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.133
they had string beans today.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.067
I just don't think
they go with Thanksgiving.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.701
-No.
-They don't grow in the fall.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.200
-They're not in season.
-The garden is over.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.701
-That is weird.
-Yeah.

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:03.200
They have string beans, and they
always have stuff on them.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.767
You know, like, almonds
and stuff like that.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:09.534
-Or what's the -- No, the other
thing they put on top.

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:12.334
Dried onions?
-Yeah, fried onions.

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:14.234
Fried onions. Terrible.

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:15.567
-I don't like
when people put things

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:18.334
on top to cover the taste.
-Not my style.

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:20.467
I don't even have a recipe
for string beans.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.334
-Oh, you know what I meant to
tell you,

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:25.667
by the way, thank you so much.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:28.734
You gave me a jar of tiny little
beautiful peppers.

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.200
-Those little Brazilian peppers.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.300
-They looked like raindrops.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.100
-Yes, red and yellow.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.434
Pickled. Pickled.

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.167
-Pickled and delicious
and I loved it.

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:38.601
-I grow those.
-You do?

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.067
-Yes.
-That was the best because

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.801
remember I ran into you
at a farm.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:44.000
-That's right. Remember?
-I was at a farm.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.234
-What's the name of
that great farm out there?

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.234
-It's Fairview Farms.
-Oh, so good.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.834
-Harry is the guy, the farmer.

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:50.901
I was at this place
and I got a pickle

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:52.200
'cause I was getting into
pickling.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.667
I go, "Harry --" to this farmer,

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.667
I go, "Do you know how to pickle
at all?

00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:56.934
I have no idea what I'm doing.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:58.801
Is there anything to do
at this cool farm?"

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:01.200
He goes, "I have no idea
how to pickle things,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.033
but you should ask her.
She would know."

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:04.467
And it was Martha Stewart.

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:06.801
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my God!

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:08.634
It was like I summoned you
there.

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:09.968
-Yep.
[ Applause ]

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:11.501
-You were really helpful.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:13.300
You went in your car.
You got your iPad.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.968
And you got into your recipe
from your website and showed me.

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:17.601
-You bought a lot of pickles
that day.

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:19.000
-I did, I did. Yeah.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.834
We went to Martha.com, which we
should talk about that.

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.534
It is your one-stop shopping
for anything holiday.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.300
Martha.com.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.534
-Except for Questlove's shoes,
those Crocs he's making.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:31.167
[ Gasps ] They light up.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.601
The little heart lights up.
Thank you, Questlove.

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:35.300
-You're welcome.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.501
-I got a pair.
-Yeah, thank you, Questlove.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:38.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:41.868
-You're welcome.
-By the way, 12 1/2, by the way.

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:45.767
Whenever you get around to it.
Take your time, buddy.

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:47.367
There's so many things
on the website,

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.100
and you curate this yourself.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.567
But one of the things I saw that
I was like,

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:52.901
"I wanted to hear about this"

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:54.334
has a very interesting
backstory.

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:57.334
You have a nativity set.
-[ Gasps ] Yes.

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:59.234
-This is a beautiful nativity
set. Look.

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:00.701
-Oh, it is. It's gilded.

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:02.667
Isn't that beautiful?
-It is gorgeous.

00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:04.601
-All the characters are there.

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:06.634
The camels
and the three wise men.

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.434
Do you know
the wise men's names?

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:11.434
You should know that.
-George?

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.601
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:16.901
-And there are Mary and Joseph
and the baby Jesus.

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:19.300
-Can you tell the story about
how this came to be?

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:23.901
-Well, I was at this very lovely
federal camp

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:28.701
down in Alderson, West Virginia.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.701 --> 00:06:30.400
They had a ceramics class.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.601
And really there's a very nice
story to this.

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:35.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:39.367
And I chose to spend my evenings
making ceramics.

00:06:39.367 --> 00:06:41.868
-Yes. Can you just plug
your ears for one second?

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:45.701
-There wasn't much more to do
at this -- Yes.

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:47.067
-Prison. Okay.

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:49.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:50.701
So, you were in camp.

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:54.701
-It was really Yale.
I was at Yale.

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:56.667
-Yes, of course.

00:06:56.667 --> 00:07:00.133
-And you can -- you can think of
other ways to say it.

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:02.634
You know, you don't have to say
the P word.

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:06.400
-You're very creative.
-Anyway, the whole --

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.634
I looked through all the --

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:10.167
They had rooms and rooms of
beautiful molds.

00:07:10.167 --> 00:07:12.667
American molds for ceramics.

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:14.033
I don't know
where they got them from.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:17.267
Oh, actually, it was a girls
college before it was a P.

00:07:17.267 --> 00:07:21.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.501 --> 00:07:26.100
And I found the entire nativity
scene, everybody,

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:29.767
including the little donkeys
and those --

00:07:29.767 --> 00:07:30.901
They're so cute.
And the little angels.

00:07:30.901 --> 00:07:33.534
-Only you would find this
in a P.

00:07:33.534 --> 00:07:36.534
-And then I was told --
I collected all the molds.

00:07:36.534 --> 00:07:38.734
And there were something
like 15 pieces.

00:07:38.734 --> 00:07:41.100
And I said, "Well, you know,
this is one set."

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.601
You're allowed to make
three things. Three.

00:07:43.601 --> 00:07:47.934
And so I persuaded the warden
that 15 pieces was one thing.

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:49.334
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:50.834
You couldn't do one and not do
all of them.

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:54.968
-You don't have to say warden.
You could say camp counselor.

00:07:54.968 --> 00:07:57.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.968 --> 00:08:01.300
-Anyway, so now
my company thought

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.701
it was a great idea
to re-create it.

00:08:03.701 --> 00:08:05.467
And we have re-created it
in white

00:08:05.467 --> 00:08:07.801
and now we re-created it
in gold.

00:08:07.801 --> 00:08:09.667
-I want to show.
This is the gold --

00:08:09.667 --> 00:08:12.701
This is the gold that you can
get off Martha.com.

00:08:12.701 --> 00:08:14.767
-That's Joseph.
-That's Joseph. It's gorgeous.

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:16.334
And this is -- This is --

00:08:16.334 --> 00:08:18.534
-Oh, don't you dare break that.
-No, no, no.

00:08:18.534 --> 00:08:19.834
-This is the original.

00:08:19.834 --> 00:08:21.000
-This is the original one
that you made.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.267
-Yes, in drab wear.

00:08:23.267 --> 00:08:24.901
Wedgewood drab wear.

00:08:24.901 --> 00:08:27.000
And here's the original --
Hello, Joseph.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.367
-Wow.
-It's pretty, right?

00:08:29.367 --> 00:08:31.467
-Yeah! That's amazing.

00:08:31.467 --> 00:08:33.534
-I mean, and look in the bottom.

00:08:34.634 --> 00:08:35.767
That's my number.

00:08:35.767 --> 00:08:44.467
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:44.467 --> 00:08:47.267
-I have to hug you.
I have to hug you.

00:08:47.267 --> 00:08:50.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:50.767 --> 00:08:52.634
Martha Stewart, everybody.
Come on!

00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:55.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:56.667
Check out Martha.com

00:08:56.667 --> 00:08:58.501
for everything you need
this holiday season.

00:08:58.501 --> 00:09:01.267
We'll be right back with a
performance from The Smile.

00:09:01.267 --> 00:09:02.300
Stick around.

